<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karakoram Highway</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as KKH</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Karakoram Highway is a road that runs from Hasan Abdal in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> through the Karakoram range and over the Khunjerab Pass to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgar">Kashgar</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Built by Pakistan and China between 1959 and 1979, it is one of the highest paved roads in the world. It passes through the Hunza valley and opened the region to trade and tourism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karakoram-highway.jpg" alt="Karakoram Highway" width="320" height="458" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: de:Benutzer:Grag, Tevatron, Lexicon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KKH.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
